## The following text has been annotated for parts of speech by students at NTU Singapore as part of a class project in AY 2025-26.
## Verses are extracted from the taggedPBC. Annotations have been developed with a combination of manual and automated approaches, with reference to existing literature and (where possible) native speakers.
## ISO 639-3: hak, Language: Hakka Chinese, Number of verses: 21
## References: Chappell, H. (2017). Languages of China in their East and Southeast Asian Context. In Cambridge University Press eBooks (pp. 651–676). https://doi.org/10.1017/9781107279872.025 ; Cortazzi, M., & Chen, W. (2026b). A Critical analysis on the revival of Hakka Diversity. Studies of Applied Linguistics in Asia, 1(1), 35–45. https://doi.org/10.53941/sala.2026.100004 ; Ministry of Education. (n.d.). Hakka Knowledge Base [Kè-yǔ Zhīshìkù]. Taiwan Hakka Dictionary [Táiwān Kè-yǔ Cídiǎn]. https://hakkadict.moe.edu.tw/

